## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of per-tenant routing, docker configs, and zero-downtime reconfiguration in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik dynamic config and weighted routing
- Docker Configs for per-tenant policy
- TLS termination at edge proxy
- Multi-DC docker-dca deployment basics
- Observability of per-tenant routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Traefik dynamic config snippet (example)
{
  "http": {
    "routers": {
      "tenant-ab": {
        "rule": "Host(`api.local`)",
        "tls": { "certResolver": "myresolver" },
        "service": "ab-backend"
      }
    },
    "services": {
      "ab-backend": {
        "loadBalancer": {
          "weighted": {
            "services": [
              { "name": "api-v1", "weight": 80 },
              { "name": "api-v2", "weight": 20 }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant weight changes in production?
- How would you handle missing or malformed ab-split entries?
- How would you monitor skew and rollback strategies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests distributed tracing setup across data centers, focusing on OpenTelemetry instrumentation, cross-DC propagation, and dynamic sampling via Docker Config rather than hard-coded values.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry instrumentation and OTLP exporters
- Cross-DC trace propagation with TraceContext
- Docker Config for per-tenant sampling rules
- Traefik TLS termination and service mesh-lite tracing
- Replicated collectors and scalable backends

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: OpenTelemetry setup sketch (Node.js) import and initialization
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');
const { registerInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider({ /* resource: tenant, service, etc. */ });
const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: process.env.OTLP_URL });
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(exporter));
provider.register();
registerInstrumentations({ tracerProvider: provider, // instrumentations
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you roll out per-tenant sampling rate changes without redeploying?
- How would you verify trace completeness across DCs during a failover?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end trust from image provenance to runtime policy enforcement, plus canary control and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Content Trust/Notary for image provenance
- SPIFFE/SVIDs via Vault for mTLS
- OPA policies loaded via Docker Config
- Sigver sidecar for per-request validation
- Canary rollout with latency/error thresholds and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: verify image signature before starting app
async function verifySignature(image) {
  const sig = await notary.verify(image);
  if (!sig || !sig.valid) throw new Error('invalid image');
  return true;
}
```

